Description: A comprehensive toolkit for quantitative ethnomedicine analysis 
    and traditional drug discovery. Implements core indices including Use 
    Value (UV), Fidelity Level (FL), Informant Consensus Factor (ICF), 
    Relative Importance (RI), Cultural Importance (CI), Medicinal Use Value 
    (MUV), Informant Agreement Ratio (IAR), and Botanical Ethnoknowledge 
    Index (BEI). Provides high-performance computing tools including parallel 
    processing, machine learning prioritization, and network pharmacology 
    visualization. Methods are based on Friedman et al. (1986), 
    Trotter and Logan (1986), Phillips and Gentry (1993), Bennett and Prance 
    (2000), Tardío and Pardo-de-Santayana (2008), and Silva et al. (2019).
